1740:
The City of Marietta adopts the following rules and regulations and any future amendments that have been adopted by the Cobb County Board of Health or the Georgia Department of Human Resources:
A. Rules and regulations for on-site sewage management systems, Chapter 290-5-26 as revised by the Department of Human Resources and as adopted by the Board of Health on August 21, 2003;
B. Ordinance concerning nuisance as adopted by the Board of Health on April 1, 1948;
C. Regulations concerning trailer parks, pursuant to the authority of O.C.G.A. § 31-3-6 and as adopted by the Board of Health on June 17, 1999;
D. Rules and regulations for food service, Chapter 290-5-14 as revised by the Department of Human Resources and as adopted by the Board of Health on June 19, 2003;
E. Rules and regulations for swimming pools, as adopted by the Board of Health on February 9, 1995; and
F. Rules and regulations for tourist accommodations, as adopted by the Board of Health on June 18, 1998.
These ordinances are on file with the city clerk and may be reviewed during normal business hours. Any amendment to these regulations shall not be effective for enforcement as a city ordinance until the amendments are placed on file with the city clerk.
(Ord. No. 5766, 11/12/97, § 1; Ord. No. 6583, 10/8/2003, § 1)
